From 9e8055e73b1be5d1269ef2811f3b88c08b3617d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:26:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-modeset: HDMI Deep Colour at 16 bits per component
 (DC_48)

HDMI defines Deep Colour at 30, 36 and 48 bits per pixel (10, 12 and
16 bits per component). The sink declares them in the HDMI VSDB of its
EDID (CTA-861: DC_30bit, DC_36bit, DC_48bit, and DC_Y444 for YCbCr 4:4:4).
The source signals the active depth in the General Control Packet's
colour depth (CD) field: CD=7 means 48 bits per pixel, and the packing
phase is 0 because a 48-bit group holds exactly one pixel (the section
number, HDMI 1.4b 6.5.3, is taken from the nouveau change and was not
re-checked against the spec). NVKMS stopped at 12 bpc, although it already parsed
DC_48.

Select 16 bpc when the sink declares DC_48, the GPU is Turing or newer
(new HAL cap supportsHDMI16BPC; nouveau gates on TU102 and newer) and
max_output_color_depth allows it:

 - add NV_KMS_DPY_ATTRIBUTE_CURRENT_COLOR_BPC_16 and
   NVKMS_PIXEL_DEPTH_48_444, with the helpers that map between them
 - nvDpyIsHdmiDepth48Evo(): DC_48, HAL cap, HDMI, module parameter;
   YCbCr 4:4:4 additionally needs DC_Y444
 - program the head with PIXEL_DEPTH_BPP_48_444
 - send CD=7 with packing phase 0 in the GCP
 - limit the pixel clock to half the single-link TMDS limit
 - no dithering at 16 bpc; DowngradeColorBpc steps 16 to 12 to 10 to 8
 - accept 16 in max_output_color_depth and make it the default; DP,
   YCbCr 4:2:2 and 4:2:0 stay capped as before; other values are
   clamped down to 6, 8, 10, 12 or 16 with a kernel log message (11 gives
   10, 13 to 15 give 12, above 16 gives 16; 0 still means 10)

Sinks that do not declare DC_48 are unchanged: nvDpyIsHdmiDepth48Evo()
is false, so the 12 and 10 bpc selection, the clock limits and the GCP
are exactly as before. HDMI FRL is not extended to 16 bpc: the FRL
query still rejects it, so such modes fall back through the downgrade.

Not verified: the module builds against our 7.3.0-rc1 headers, nothing
more. The closed GSP firmware may reject or ignore a 48 bpp head
depth. No 48-bit sink is at hand (our TVs declare only DC_30 and
DC_36), so 16 bpc has never run on hardware. The register values come
from the nouveau change (head BPP_48_444, GCP CD=7), itself untested.

Assisted-by: claude-sonnet (Claude Code subagent)
